Protect Codex sessions, archived sessions, state databases and thread-history databases from general cleanup. Explicitly authorized session repair requires a dry run, consistent backups, affected-task inventory, source preservation and an application reopen check. Never use rollout migration as a cleanup shortcut.

## 6. Evidence, acceptance and delivery

Use the smallest decisive verification, broadening when shared contracts or downstream consumers are affected. Deterministic checks and actual runtime state can close low-risk objective work. Apply Section 2 to determine when independent model review is required; maintain source-based and runtime evidence even when dispatch is excluded. Model confidence, a passing test count or a generated file alone does not prove the whole task complete.

