13:## 2. Scale the work
14:
15:- Direct: bounded, low-consequence work with clear evidence. Inspect, act, verify and finish.
16:- Tracked: work with multiple phases, meaningful uncertainty or recovery cost. Keep one concise plan/checkpoint and verify material outcomes.
17:- Controlled: high-consequence, externally consequential, regulated or difficult-to-recover work. Make authority, evidence and recovery explicit.
18:
19:Risk determines evidence and authority requirements. Neither “minimum process” nor task size determines delegation by itself. At the start of non-trivial work, choose direct, execution, conference, or execution-plus-conference and record one sentence explaining why in the existing checkpoint. Do not create a separate planning artifact for this decision. Reconsider only after a material scope/risk change, two failures without new evidence, or a persistent context/verification bottleneck.
